# Tailwind CSS v4 Standards for Rails 7.2

<rule>
name: tailwind_v4
description: Standards for Tailwind CSS v4 usage in Rails 7.2
filters:
  - type: file_extension
    pattern: "\\.(css|erb)$"
  - type: directory
    pattern: "(app/assets/stylesheets|app/assets/builds|app/javascript)"
actions:
  - type: suggest
    message: |
      1. Directory Structure (Rails 7.2):
         ```
         app/
         ├── assets/
         │   ├── stylesheets/
         │   │   └── application.css    # Main Tailwind input file
         │   └── builds/
         │       └── tailwind.css       # Generated output file
         └── javascript/
             └── application.js         # JavaScript entry point
         ```

      2. Development Process:
         - Use bin/dev for development
         - Run rails tailwindcss:build before deployment
         - Check if styles are applied before committing
         - Never modify the generated tailwind.css file directly

      3. Configuration Requirements:
         - All Tailwind customizations go in app/assets/stylesheets/application.css
         - Use @layer components { } for component styles
         - Use @layer utilities { } for custom utilities
         - Use @apply for extracting common utility patterns
         - Add plugins via @import statements at the top of application.css
         - Example structure:
           ```css
           @tailwind base;
           @tailwind components;
           @tailwind utilities;

           /* Custom plugins and imports */
           @import "@tailwindcss/forms";
           @import "@tailwindcss/typography";
           @import "@tailwindcss/container-queries";

           /* Custom component styles */
           @layer components {
             .btn-primary {
               @apply px-4 py-2 bg-blue-500 text-white rounded-lg hover:bg-blue-600;
             }
           }

           /* Custom utilities */
           @layer utilities {
             .scrollbar-hide {
               scrollbar-width: none;
             }
           }
           ```

      4. Layout Requirements (Rails 7.2):
         ```erb
         <%= stylesheet_link_tag "tailwind", "data-turbo-track": "reload" %>
         <%= stylesheet_link_tag "application", "data-turbo-track": "reload" %>
         ```

      5. Rails 7.2 Specific Notes:
         - Use Sprockets or importmap-rails for asset management
         - Configure tailwindcss-rails gem properly
         - Ensure proper asset precompilation in production
         - Use bin/dev for development server
</rule>

